diff --git a/docs/timer.md b/docs/timer.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..54bbf2a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/timer.md
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# Quizzy – Timer Design Notes
+
+## Requirements Recap
+- Quiz settings add "Timer minutes" and "Timer seconds" (numbers, 0 by default). 0:00 means no timer.
+- With a timer: moderator's big screen shows countdown in M:SS (e.g., "1:30", "0:05") while question is open. Players don't see timer.
+- Countdown starts when question opens. Reloading doesn't restart it.
+- At 0:00, question finishes by itself, as if moderator clicked "Finish". Moderator can still click "Finish" earlier.
+- Timer is setting of this Quizzy, not part of export format.
+
+## Data Model (migration 20261008130001)
+- `quizzes.timer_minutes` + `timer_seconds` integer NOT NULL DEFAULT 0. Model validates presence + integer >=0. Relies on DB default for `Quiz.new` (0). Form uses `value="<%= h @quiz.timer_minutes %>"` so new shows 0, validation errors preserve typed value. Blank ("") typecasts to nil → invalid ("can't be blank").
+- No new game columns: reuses `games.opened_at` (set to `Time.current` on `start!`/`next_question!`) + live quiz duration. Countdown = `opened_at + total` where `total = minutes*60+seconds`. Reload-safe because `opened_at` persists.
+- `Quiz#timer_total_seconds` / `#timer_enabled?` helpers (total>0). `Game` delegates live (reads `quiz.timer_*` or `quiz.timer_total_seconds`, fallback 0 if missing).
+- Export (`Quizzes#export`) unchanged: only `{title, questions:[{text,active,options:[{text,correct}]}]}`. Import ignores unknown keys, so timer never exported/imported.
+
+## Game Timer Helpers (`Game`)
+- `timer_total_seconds`: live quiz total, clamped >=0, 0 if no quiz/missing cols.
+- `timer_enabled?`: total>0.
+- `expires_at`: `opened_at + total.seconds` if open+enabled+opened_at, else nil.
+- `seconds_remaining(now=Time.current)`: `ceil(expires - now)`, clamped >=0, nil if no timer/not open. Ceil so 4.1s shows "0:05", 0 shows "0:00".
+- `Game.format_timer(sec)`: `"#{sec/60}:#{(sec%60).to_s.rjust(2,'0')}"` → "1:30", "0:05", "0:00", "10:00". Shared by server view + state JSON.
+- `timer_text(now)`: formatted remaining or nil.
+- `timer_expired?(now)`: open+enabled+opened_at && now>=expires.
+- `expire_open_question_if_needed!(now)`: if expired → `finish_question!` (transaction+reload, idempotent). Called server-side on every game access.
+- `content_version`: now `"#{status}|#{index}|#{winners}|#{winners_count}|#{timer_total}"` (added timer_total). Remaining NOT in version (would reload every second). Total in version triggers reload when quiz setting changes mid-open (timer appears/disappears/extends).
+
+## Live / Polling
+- Big screen (`moderate/games/show` + `_screen` + `Games#state/content`):
+  - `prepare_screen_vars` reloads game+quiz, calls `expire_open_question_if_needed!` before rendering (reload-safe), sets `@timer_enabled/@timer_text/@timer_remaining/@timer_total/@timer_expires_at_ms/@server_now_ms` when open+enabled.
+  - `_screen` open branch renders `<div class="timer-countdown" id="question-timer" data-expires-at-ms data-server-now-ms data-remaining> M:SS </div>` only when enabled+open. Closed/lobby/finished never render it.
+  - `state.json` when open+enabled adds `timer_enabled:true, timer_total, timer_remaining, timer_text, timer_expires_at_ms, server_now_ms`; else `timer_enabled:false`. Closed/lobby/finished also false.
+  - JS polls state every 250ms (existing `cleanUrl` for userinfo), compares `content_version` (fallback status/index), fetches `content.html` on change and calls `initTimerFromDom()`. When version unchanged, updates `players/answers` counters in-place + `updateTimerFromState(data)` (updates deadline + text from server, handles timer appear/disappear). Separate 250ms `tickTimer()` ticks locally via `deadlineClient = expiresMs - (serverNow - Date.now())` and `ceil((deadline-Date.now())/1000)` formatted as M:SS, so countdown moves smoothly even if fetch blips. At 0 server closes on next state poll (≤250ms), version open→closed triggers content reload to closed view (no timer, Correct+counts+Next/End).
+  - Reload: server recomputes remaining from `opened_at`, so reloaded page shows decreased time, not full duration. JS re-inits deadline from new DOM data attributes.
+- Phones (`play/show` + `_content` + `Play#state/content/answer`):
+  - `prepare_player_vars` + `join`/`answer` reload game+quiz and call `expire_open_question_if_needed!` before logic, so players' polling also triggers auto-close even if big screen closed. `answer` after expiry is rejected as closed (422 JSON, then polls to closed feedback).
+  - `state.json` remains `{version,status}` only (no timer leak). `content.html` has no timer markup. Verified: open player shows question+options, no `question-timer`/`timer-countdown`.
+  - After auto-finish, players auto-follow open→closed via 250ms version polling (`open-idx` → `closed-idx`), showing "Correct!"/"Wrong!"/"No answer" without reload.
+
+## Views / Labels (exact)
+- Quiz form (`_form.html.erb`): `<label for="quiz_timer_minutes">Timer minutes</label>` + `<input id="quiz_timer_minutes" name="quiz[timer_minutes]" type="number" min="0" step="1" required placeholder/aria>` and same for `quiz_timer_seconds`. Both 0 by default on new, preserve on edit/error.
+- Big screen open (`_screen.html.erb`): timer div as above, styled `.timer-countdown` (yellow pill, big display font, `min-width:3.2em`). Only when open+enabled.
+- No points/timer leak: open big screen shows no counts/Correct; open player shows no timer/points; state JSONs never include correct/points.
+
+## Routes / Controllers
+- No new routes. `Games#state/content/show` + `Play#state/content/show/join/answer` all call expiry check. `Games#state` adds timer fields (moderator only). `Play` adds no timer fields.
+- `Quizzes#quiz_params` permits `:timer_minutes, :timer_seconds`. `Quizzes#export` unchanged (no timer).
+
+## QA Notes
+- Lists: question/quiz/leaderboard still `<li>` scoped; switches still checkboxes; deletes still native confirm (unchanged).
+- M:SS via `Game.format_timer` (server) + `formatTimer()` (JS) guarantees "1:30" vs "0:05" vs "0:00".
+- No timer (0:00): no `#question-timer` element, `timer_enabled:false`, stays open until manual Finish, no auto-close.
+- At 0:00: brief "0:00" then auto-reload to closed (same as Finish). Manual Finish earlier still works (closes immediately, timer gone).
+- Reload persistence: `opened_at` stable, remaining decreases; tested 0:07→0:05→reload 0:04, 1:30→1:29.
+- Players never see timer: no element, no text, no JSON field; verified in browser.
+
+## Future
+- If quiz timer edited mid-open, expiry moves live (opened_at + new total) and content reloads via version change (intentional, like winners_count live).
+- Seconds >59 allowed (e.g., 0:90 → 1:30 display); no upper bound validation.
+- Sub-second precision: server uses float+ceil, client uses ms+ceil; ≤250ms polling ensures all screens close ~simultaneously.
